# Template for .env.production (which is gitignored). Copy it and fill in real
# values:  cp .env.production.example .env.production
#
# deploy.sh reads .env.production and pushes each line to the Worker as a SECRET
# (`pywrangler secret put KEY`). Secrets persist across deploys; plaintext vars do
# not (a deploy that omits them wipes them), which is why these aren't [vars].
#
# Exception: CLOUDFLARE_* keys configure wrangler itself (not the Worker), so
# deploy.sh exports them and does NOT push them as secrets.

# The Cloudflare account to deploy to. Kept here (gitignored) rather than in the
# committed wrangler.toml so this open-source repo doesn't ship a specific account
# ID and forks deploy to their own account. Find yours: `wrangler whoami`.
CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=your-cloudflare-account-id

# Cloudflare API token for NON-INTERACTIVE deploys (CI, a headless box, an agent).
# On a workstation `wrangler login` (cached OAuth) is enough and this can stay
# unset. But with no TTY wrangler can't open that login, so it fails — after the
# build has already run migrate.sh — with:
#   Failed to fetch auth token: 400 Bad Request
#   ...necessary to set a CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN environment variable...
# Create a scoped token (permissions: Account > Workers Scripts: Edit, and
# Account > D1: Edit) and set it here; deploy.sh exports it for wrangler (it is
# NOT pushed as a Worker secret). Leave it unset to use interactive OAuth instead.
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/fundamentals/api/get-started/create-token/
# CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=

# Optional, separately scoped token used only to attach a sanitized excerpt of
# the prior two minutes of Workers Logs to non-green component-attention email.
# Do not reuse the deployment token above. Grant only Account > Workers
# Observability: Write for this account. deploy.sh maps these two CLOUDFLARE_*
# configuration values to Worker secrets without exposing either in
# wrangler.toml. Alerts still send with an "unavailable" note if omitted.
# CLOUDFLARE_OBSERVABILITY_API_TOKEN=
# WORKERS_OBSERVABILITY_SERVICE=forkmesh-relay

# Admin error dashboard at https://<host>/<ADMIN_PATH>. Access is gated by a
# forkmesh login whose account has the is_admin flag (set it in the DB:
# UPDATE accounts SET is_admin=1 WHERE name='<node>'), not a static password.
# ADMIN_PATH must start with "admin-" so it is routed to the worker.
ADMIN_PATH=admin-CHANGE-ME-TO-SOMETHING-RANDOM

# At-rest encryption key for D1: derives the AES-GCM data key AND the blind-index
# HMAC key. Some historical encrypted rows may still contain frozen legacy
# wallet seeds until the explicit offline custody migration exports, reconciles,
# and scrubs them. No live Worker path can use those seeds. DATA_KEY must remain
# a strong Worker secret and MUST NOT live in wrangler.toml [vars].
# Generate one with:  python3 -c "import secrets;print(secrets.token_urlsafe(48))"
# Rotating it makes existing encrypted rows undecryptable. Complete and verify
# docs/operations/legacy-solana-custody-migration.md before any rotation.
DATA_KEY=CHANGE-ME-RUN-THE-GENERATOR-ABOVE

# Direct-HTTPS mirror request capability identity. This is an infrastructure
# signing key, not a user/wallet/repository key. The 32-byte seed is pushed as a
# Worker secret and is never stored in D1; mirror gateways receive only the
# public key (GET /api/mirrors/https). Keep both values from the same Ed25519
# keypair, base64url without padding. See
# docs/operations/direct-https-mirror-gateway.md for a generation command.
MIRROR_ROUTER_PUBLIC_KEY=CHANGE-ME-BASE64URL-32-BYTE-PUBLIC-KEY
MIRROR_ROUTER_SIGNING_SEED=CHANGE-ME-BASE64URL-32-BYTE-SEED

# Production rewards are mainnet-only by default. The committed production
# Worker config supplies mainnet-beta and its public RPC; set the public pool
# address and signer account here. Existing ForkMesh one-click deployments use
# TREASURY_SOLANA_ADDRESS. COMMUNITY_REWARD_POOL_ADDRESS is the optional modern
# override and takes priority when non-empty. Both values are public addresses
# only. At runtime ForkMesh verifies the RPC genesis hash and that the account
# exists on that cluster before exposing or scheduling the pool. Never put the
# pool private key, seed phrase, or signed transaction here.
TREASURY_SOLANA_ADDRESS=CHANGE-ME-PUBLIC-MAINNET-ADDRESS
# COMMUNITY_REWARD_POOL_ADDRESS=<optional-explicit-public-mainnet-address>
# REWARD_SIGNER_ACCOUNT=<first-instance-owner-account>

# Optional node-side Git SSH gateway. A Cloudflare HTTP Worker cannot terminate
# raw SSH, so SSH_GATEWAY_HOST must point (through DNS plus a TCP-capable edge
# product such as Cloudflare Spectrum, or directly) to an independently operated
# OpenSSH origin running tools/ssh_gateway.py. SSH URLs remain hidden until a
# valid host, port, shared authorization token, and exact repository allowlist
# are all configured. Generate the allowlist from the node-side config with
# `python3 tools/ssh_gateway.py --config /etc/forkmesh/ssh-gateway.json
# worker-allowlist`; do not list a repository until that gateway actually has
# the corresponding local bare repository.
# Generate the 32–512 character base64url token with:
# python3 -c "import secrets;print(secrets.token_urlsafe(48))"
# Keep the same token in the gateway's owner-only token file. This token is
# infrastructure authorization material, never an SSH private key.
# SSH_GATEWAY_HOST=ssh.forkmesh.com
# SSH_GATEWAY_PORT=22
# SSH_GATEWAY_TOKEN=CHANGE-ME-RUN-THE-GENERATOR-ABOVE
# SSH_GATEWAY_REPOSITORIES=alice-node/widget=read-write,alice-node/docs=read-only
# Optional per-node DNS/IP overrides for independently operated gateways.
# SSH_GATEWAY_NODE_HOSTS=alice-node=ssh-alice.example.org,bob-node=192.0.2.20
# To disable an already configured gateway without relying on secret deletion,
# set SSH_GATEWAY_REPOSITORIES=disabled and repush secrets; invalid/empty
# allowlists fail closed and suppress every SSH URL.

# Mailtrap API token for transactional email (signup email confirmation). Pushed
# as a Worker secret by deploy.sh, which lists it as REQUIRED so a production
# deploy fails loudly if it's missing. The Worker reads env.MAILTRAP_API_TOKEN;
# if it's ever unset at runtime, email sending no-ops and signups fall back to
# the admin verification queue. A fork that doesn't send email can drop
# MAILTRAP_API_TOKEN from the `required` list in deploy.sh.
# Get a token: Mailtrap -> Sending Domains -> API Tokens.
MAILTRAP_API_TOKEN=CHANGE-ME
# Optional overrides (sensible defaults if omitted):
#   MAILTRAP_SENDER       From address (default no-reply@forkmesh.com)
#   MAILTRAP_SENDER_NAME  From display name (default ForkMesh)
#   MAILTRAP_API_URL      Send endpoint (default https://send.api.mailtrap.io/api/send)
# MAILTRAP_SENDER=no-reply@forkmesh.com
# MAILTRAP_SENDER_NAME=ForkMesh

# Optional read-only X API v2 bearer token. The World Twitter/X board first
# attempts X's public profile syndication page without credentials. If that
# public embed returns no posts, this token resolves @forkmesh and reads its
# recent public posts through the official users/:id/tweets endpoint. Keep it
# scoped to public-read access; the Worker never posts, replies, or stores it.
# X_API_BEARER_TOKEN=

# Optional Sentry DSN. When set as a Worker secret/var, unhandled Worker errors,
# returned 5xx responses, and cron failures are reported via direct HTTP ingest
# (no Python package or framework plugin). Request metadata is minimized and
# private-repository routes/details are redacted. Cron monitor check-in helpers
# are configured below but their live scheduled call sites remain disabled.
# SENTRY_DSN=https://PUBLIC_KEY@o000000.ingest.sentry.io/000000
# SENTRY_CRON_MONITOR_SLUG=forkmesh-relay
# SENTRY_CRON_CHECKIN_MARGIN_MINUTES=1
# SENTRY_CRON_MAX_RUNTIME_MINUTES=5
# SENTRY_CRON_TIMEZONE=UTC
